|errata_history=This is version PC-E1 (2 of 3), 14 May 2020. It is not the current version; the current version is [[Fanfare (Tatooine) (V) (Errata 2)]] (PC-E2). The image is the PC card image of this version.
* '''Original''' ([[Fanfare (Tatooine) (V)]]): PC card image of 8 July 2018<ref name="ht-D_fanfaretatooine-0">PC card image in the PC's Holotable image set: [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/blob/022435b/Images-HT/starwars/ResetDS-Dark/large/fanfaretatooine.gif fanfaretatooine.gif], commit [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/commit/022435b 022435b] (8 July 2018, “Set 9 load”).</ref>, no errata mark; lower-left name “•Fanfare (V)”. The PC first released this shield with [[Virtual Set 0]] / [[Virtual Set D]] on 24 September 2014. The PC's Holotable image set starts on 8 July 2018, so this is the earliest surviving PC card image; whether the 2014 release slip had the same words is not shown by it. Text: “Plays on table. Cancels Order To Engage and Scramble. Once per game, may ▲ an Immediate Effect. While opponent occupies no battleground systems, Staging Areas is suspended. “Missing” on Lost In The Wilderness is treated as “landspeed = 0 for remainder of turn.””
* '''PC-E1''' (this page): PC card image of 14 May 2020<ref name="ht-D_fanfaretatooine-1">PC card image in the PC's Holotable image set: [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/blob/b2c2653/Images-HT/starwars/ResetDS-Dark/large/fanfaretatooine.gif fanfaretatooine.gif], commit [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/commit/b2c2653 b2c2653] (14 May 2020, “Fix fanfare (V) shield images”).</ref>, marked “E”; lower-left name “Fanfare”. What changed from the previous version: PC errata (image marked “E”; commit “Fix fanfare (V) shield images”): Ice Storm, Lost In The Wilderness, Order To Engage, Sandwhirl and Scramble are now canceled; the “Missing” sentence is removed; “While opponent occupies no battleground systems” becomes “Unless opponent occupies a battleground system”. The lower-left name is now just “Fanfare” (no bullet, no “(V)”), and the image is re-made at a larger size. The set icon at the lower right changes from the diamond-shaped D to the round Virtual Set D icon; at the upper right the round orange icon is replaced by the Reflections III icon (the Episode I icon stays), and the red tint of the frame is gone. On this date the PC gave the Tatooine-base and Reflections III-base files the same image (one file, byte-identical); it was published again unchanged on 12 July 2020 (“March Errata Images”). Text: “Plays on table. Ice Storm, Lost In The Wilderness, Order To Engage, Sandwhirl, and Scramble are canceled. Once per game, may ▲ an Immediate Effect. Unless opponent occupies a battleground system, Staging Areas is suspended.”
* '''PC-E2''' ([[Fanfare (Tatooine) (V) (Errata 2)]]): PC card image of 31 July 2022<ref name="ht-D_fanfaretatooine-2">PC card image in the PC's Holotable image set: [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/blob/ab74419/Images-HT/starwars/ResetDS-Dark/large/fanfaretatooine.gif fanfaretatooine.gif], commit [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/commit/ab74419 ab74419] (31 July 2022, “updated hires gifs”); high-resolution image <code>ResetDS-Dark/hires/fanfaretatooine.png</code>, commit [https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/commit/594c3a0 594c3a0] (31 July 2022, “Set 0 Hi Res”).</ref>, marked “E1”; lower-left name “Fanfare (Tatooine)”. What changed from the previous version: re-rendered by the PC in its high-resolution card style (new frame, colours and typesetting); same words. The lower-left name now reads “Fanfare (Tatooine)” and the errata mark is printed as “E1”. The printed errata mark (“E1”) does not match this version's place in the release order (change 2 of this card): recorded as a [[Players Committee transcription errors#Errata marks that do not match the version (Virtual Modern)|PC transcription error]]. Text: “Plays on table. Ice Storm, Lost In The Wilderness, Order To Engage, Sandwhirl, and Scramble are canceled. Once per game, may ▲ an Immediate Effect. Unless opponent occupies a battleground system, Staging Areas is suspended.”
Versions follow Bill's rulings of 12 November 2026: every visible change on a PC card image is a version, numbered in release order; a printed errata mark that does not match that order is recorded as a PC transcription error.

